00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:08.660 align:start position:0%
Jerusalem a holy city two three major  religions is just one bone of contention  in the Middle East conflict the border  between Israel and the Palestinian west  bank runs through the city but Israel  claims the whole of Jerusalem for itself  and the Palestinians want East Jerusalem  as the capital of their future state  this is the Western Wall the holiest  site for the Jews but almost equal  numbers of Israelis and Arabs live in  the area the situation throughout the  West Bank is equally complicated more  than 600,000 Israelis live in the  territory spread over hundreds of  official and illegal settlements and the  Israeli settlers keep on building  clearing the settlements would be a  political ordeal for Israel they also  make any potential boundary between  Israel and the West Bank even more  complicated the Palestinians insist on  the borders that existed before the  six-day war in 1967 but by building  border fortifications over the past  decade seen here in yellow Israel has  moved further away from the pre-war  boundaries these walls mainly found in  the West Bank are meant to keep out  bombers from the Palestinian territories  with evidence success because the number  of attacks in Israel has decreased  significantly  the biggest security risk facing Israel  today comes from the gaza strip along  with the West Bank the territory is  intended to be part of the new  Palestinian state but if there are  negotiations who will sit at the other  side of the table in Gaza the radical  Islamic Hamas movement has been in  control since 2007 it regards Israel as  an enemy and rejects peace talks in  contrast to the more moderate Fattah  that governs the West Bank Israelis and  Palestinians are now hoping to take  first steps but neither side thinks a  solution to the Middle East conflict is  likely
 

